---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
import { groups } from "../../data/settings";
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/?$/, "/");
---
<DocsLayout title="Make it feel like you." section="settings" summary="A practical guide to the settings center: change the look, shape your workspaces, choose default applications, and understand which controls belong to your host desktop.">
  <div class="doc-callout"><p><strong>Start with the panel gear.</strong> You can also right-click the wallpaper or run <code>ludashctl open-settings</code> inside LuDash. Use the sidebar search to find a category. Most desktop preferences save immediately; JSON editors have an explicit Save button.</p></div>
  <nav class="doc-toc" aria-label="On this page">{groups.map(group => <a href={`#${group.id}`}>{group.name.split(" & ")[0]}</a>)}</nav>
  {groups.map(group => <section id={group.id}><h2>{group.name}</h2><p>{group.description}</p><ul>{group.details.map(detail => <li>{detail}</li>)}</ul></section>)}
  <CodeBlock label="DEFAULT APPLICATION EXAMPLES" code={'# Use your preferred applications\nludashctl default-apps \'{"terminal":["konsole","-e","fish"],"files":["dolphin"]}\'\n\n# Restore LunaDash Files and the LunaDash Fish terminal profile\nludashctl default-apps \'{"terminal":[],"files":[]}\'\nludashctl launch-default terminal'} />
  <h2 id="display-controls">Display and startup</h2>
  <p>Display settings control an available backlight through brightnessctl, provide a separate DDC/CI brightness slider for each compatible external monitor through ddcutil, and expose the primary output's supported resolution, refresh rate and scale. Confirm a new display configuration within 15 seconds or it reverts automatically. Nested sessions keep physical monitor modes under the host desktop's control; external brightness controls require DDC/CI enabled in the monitor menu and permission to access its I2C device. Refresh monitors after reconnecting a display or changing permissions.</p>
  <p>The desktop shows an animated LunaDash startup screen while its initial state and wallpaper load, with a minimum visible interval counted from the first rendered frame. Shell startup no longer waits for portal theme queries. Installed sessions use their installed interface files, and the settings regression check opens every page in all four bundled languages. Hidden panels load on demand and native window effects follow output frame callbacks. These changes still need hardware checks for physical display switching and actual FPS.</p>
  <h2 id="window-motion">Window animations</h2>
  <p>Switching to an offscreen window slides its column into view. Overlapping windows use a subtle focus fade. Maximizing and restoring smoothly resize the window, and closing shrinks and fades the last frame. Rapid switching continues from the current visible position.</p>
  <p>In Appearance settings, use Animations and Animation duration to adjust motion. The default is 220 ms. Turning animations off applies changes immediately. Effects follow the display's frame callbacks, and resizing does not repeatedly relayout the application on every frame.</p>
  <h2 id="app-compatibility">Application compatibility</h2>
  <p>Native application menus keep their pointer grab without repeated focus updates on each click. Discord's input helper also needs an X11 connection while its main window uses Wayland. Launch Discord through LunaDash's application menu so the authenticated XWayland service is ready; its helper root stays hidden. Direct terminal launches bypass this preparation. The Discord-only software rendering fallback remains available, but GPU flags alone cannot fix the helper's missing connection.</p>
  <p>Taskbar icons follow application IDs and installed desktop entries. Changing a document or tab title does not change the app icon. Selecting a task restores its window, changes workspace when needed and scrolls its column into view. Group highlights follow the focused member.</p>
  <p>File dialogs require xdg-desktop-portal and xdg-desktop-portal-gtk alongside the LunaDash backend. Hardware and full Discord compatibility still need real-session verification.</p>
  <h2 id="screenshots">Select a screenshot region</h2>
  <p>Press <strong>Meta+Shift+S</strong>, drag a rectangle and release to save it to Pictures/Screenshots. Escape cancels. Install grim and slurp for this feature. The control command <code>lunadashctl screenshot</code> starts selection asynchronously; <code>capture /absolute/path.png</code> retains full-output capture for automation.</p>
  <p>The selection overlay opens immediately. Pressing the shortcut again keeps the current selection, and Escape closes it without saving a file or showing an error. After updating the compositor, log out and back in to use the corrected shortcut behavior.</p>
  <h2 id="saved">Where preferences live</h2><p>Desktop settings use <code>~/.config/LuDash/LuDash.conf</code>, respecting <code>XDG_CONFIG_HOME</code>. Shell module JSON lives beside it as <code>shell-modules.json</code>. Custom QML belongs in the sibling <code>modules/</code> directory. Module code is disabled until explicitly trusted.</p>
  <CodeBlock label="APPLY A DESKTOP CHANGE" code={'ludashctl appearance \'{"accent":"#c4b5fd","gap":16,"blur":true,"blurRadius":18}\'\nludashctl open-settings appearance'} />
  <p>Each block can also have its own dimensions, color and corner radius. Follow <a href={`${base}docs/modules/`}>the module guide</a> for the JSON schema, a visual style playground, user QML and recovery commands.</p>
  <h2 id="files">A calmer file browser</h2><p>LunaDash Files uses a consistent outline icon set, a compact action toolbar, a location field and a spacious icon view. Alt+Left/Right navigates history, Alt+Up goes to the parent, Ctrl+L edits the location, and F2 renames one item. Accent changes also update open Files windows.</p><p>Copy supports regular files. Moves and Trash operations run off the UI thread; existing destinations are not overwritten. Folder copying, cross-application clipboard integration, tabs, archive tools, recursive search and network shares are still incomplete.</p>
</DocsLayout>
